---
/**
 * The salary hike calculator: a raise on CTC turned into the change in monthly in-hand pay, with
 * the tables and the "raise that costs you" example computed at build time by the engine.
 */
import DocLayout from '../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
import NumberField from '../components/form/NumberField.astro';
import SelectField from '../components/form/SelectField.astro';
import { bracketPath, lakhs } from '../lib/brackets';
import { formatCompactRupees, formatRupees } from '../lib/format';
import { calculatorLink, compareHike, renderHike } from '../lib/hike';
import { DEFAULT_INPUT } from '../lib/tax/defaults';
import { cityOptionsHtml } from '../lib/city-options';
import { STATES } from '../lib/tax/professional-tax';

const STATE = DEFAULT_INPUT.stateCode;
const CITY = DEFAULT_INPUT.city;
const START = lakhs(10);
const HIKE = 20;
const initial = renderHike({
  ctc: START,
  newCtc: Math.round(START * (1 + HIKE / 100)),
  stateCode: STATE,
  city: CITY,
});

const at = (from: number, to: number) => compareHike(from, to, STATE, CITY)!;
const pct = (fraction: number) => `${(Math.round(fraction * 1000) / 10).toFixed(1)}%`;

const HIKES = [10, 20, 30];
const table = [6, 8, 10, 12, 15, 20, 25, 30, 40, 50].map((lpa) => {
  const ctc = lakhs(lpa);
  return {
    lpa,
    now: at(ctc, ctc + 1).before.monthly,
    cells: HIKES.map((h) => at(ctc, Math.round(ctc * (1 + h / 100)))),
  };
});
const row = (lpa: number) => table.find((r) => r.lpa === lpa)!;
const low = row(10).cells[1];
const edge = row(12).cells[1];
const high = row(50).cells[0];

// The ₹50,000 raise above ₹12.5 lakh that costs the most in-hand pay.
let worst = at(lakhs(12.5), lakhs(12.5) + 50_000);
for (let ctc = lakhs(12.5); ctc <= lakhs(15); ctc += 5_000) {
  const o = at(ctc, ctc + 50_000);
  if (o.monthlyGain < worst.monthlyGain) worst = o;
}
const worstYear = Math.abs(Math.round(worst.split.inHand));
---

<DocLayout
  title="Salary hike calculator: what your raise adds in hand"
  description="Turn a hike on your CTC into the change in your monthly in-hand salary for FY 2026-27, with income tax, PF and professional tax for your state, and see where the extra money goes."
  updated="2026-10-16"
  ogImage="salary-hike-calculator"
  about={['Salary hike', 'In-hand salary', 'Income tax']}
  deva="कमाई"
>
  <p>
    A hike is quoted on your CTC, but what you feel is the change in your monthly in-hand pay. The
    two are rarely the same: income tax, provident fund and the ₹12 lakh rebate all move between
    them. Enter your current CTC and the hike, or the new CTC from your offer letter.
  </p>

  <form
    id="hike"
    class="panel not-prose overflow-clip"
    novalidate
    aria-label="Salary hike calculator"
  >
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-x-8 gap-y-5 p-5 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <NumberField
        id="h-ctc"
        label="Current CTC"
        value={START.toLocaleString('en-IN')}
        prefix="₹"
        width="7.5rem"
        hint="A year"
        money
      />
      <NumberField
        id="h-pct"
        label="Hike"
        value={String(HIKE)}
        suffix="%"
        width="3.5rem"
        inputmode="decimal"
        hint="Or type the new CTC below"
      />
      <NumberField
        id="h-new"
        label="New CTC"
        value={Math.round(START * (1 + HIKE / 100)).toLocaleString('en-IN')}
        prefix="₹"
        width="7.5rem"
        hint="Updates with the hike, and the other way round"
        money
      />
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3">
        <SelectField id="h-state" label="Work state">
          {STATES.map((s) => (
            <option value={s.code} selected={s.code === STATE}>
              {s.name}
            </option>
          ))}
        </SelectField>
        <SelectField id="h-city" label="City">
          <Fragment set:html={cityOptionsHtml(STATE, CITY)} />
        </SelectField>
      </div>
    </div>
    <output
      id="h-result"
      for="h-ctc h-pct h-new h-state h-city"
      class="block border-t border-line result-wash p-5 sm:p-6"
      aria-live="polite"
      set:html={initial}
    />
  </form>

  <p>
    Both salaries use the calculator's standard structure: Basic at half of CTC, PF at the statutory
    ceiling and gratuity inside CTC, with each side taking whichever regime is cheaper. If your
    offer is structured differently, put the new CTC into the <a href="/">full calculator</a> and
    match each component.
  </p>

  <h2>What a hike adds in hand</h2>
  <p>
    The extra in-hand pay a month, and how much your in-hand rises in percent, for hikes of 10%, 20%
    and 30% on common salaries, in Bengaluru.
  </p>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Current CTC</th>
          <th scope="col">In hand now</th>
          {HIKES.map((h) => (
            <th scope="col">{h}% hike</th>
          ))}
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {table.map((r) => (
          <tr>
            <td>
              <a href={bracketPath(r.lpa)}>{r.lpa} LPA</a>
            </td>
            <td>{formatRupees(r.now)}</td>
            {r.cells.map((o) => (
              <td>
                +{formatRupees(o.monthlyGain)} <span class="text-ink-3">({pct(o.inHandHike)})</span>
              </td>
            ))}
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Why your in-hand rise is not your hike</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Up to about ₹12 lakh, in-hand rises a little faster than CTC.</strong> There is no
      income tax yet, and PF at the statutory ceiling and professional tax stay the same as your pay
      grows. A 20% hike on {formatCompactRupees(low.before.ctc)} raises in-hand pay by{' '}
      {pct(low.inHandHike)}.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Crossing ₹12 lakh of taxable income ends the rebate.</strong> Above the limit the full
      slab tax applies, eased only at first by marginal relief, so a raise across it loses a large
      share to tax. A 20% hike on {formatCompactRupees(edge.before.ctc)} raises in-hand pay by only{' '}
      {pct(edge.inHandHike)}.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Above ₹50 lakh, surcharge starts.</strong> A 10% hike on{' '}
      {formatCompactRupees(high.before.ctc)} raises in-hand pay by {pct(high.inHandHike)}, because
      the 10% surcharge begins once taxable income passes ₹50 lakh.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>PF and gratuity grow with Basic.</strong> Part of every raise goes into your provident
      fund and the gratuity provision. That money is still yours, just not in this month's salary.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When a raise leaves you with less</h2>
  <p>
    Just above ₹12 lakh of taxable income, the rebate tapers off rather than stopping dead: your tax
    is capped at the income above the limit. The 4% cess is still charged on top, so inside this
    band each extra rupee of income costs slightly more than a rupee in tax.
  </p>
  <p>
    With the standard structure, a raise of ₹50,000 from {formatCompactRupees(worst.before.ctc)} to{' '}
    {formatCompactRupees(worst.after.ctc)} adds {formatRupees(worst.split.tax)} of income tax and
    leaves you <strong>{formatRupees(worstYear)} a year worse off</strong>. Past the band, a raise
    is taxed at the ordinary slab rates again and in-hand pay climbs normally.
  </p>
  <p>
    If a raise would land you in this band, it is worth asking payroll whether part of it can be
    paid as an employer contribution to NPS, which the new regime still lets you deduct (section
    124), or simply negotiating a raise large enough to clear it. The{' '}
    <a href="/marginal-relief">marginal relief guide</a> shows the band in detail.
  </p>

  <h2>Next steps</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href={calculatorLink(lakhs(12), STATE, CITY)}>See any new CTC broken down in full</a>, with
      both regimes, every deduction and a PDF to keep.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/compare-offers">Compare two offers side by side</a> if the raise comes with a move
      to a new company.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/old-vs-new-tax-regime">Check which regime suits you</a> once your salary changes.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/in-hand-salary">In-hand salary at every CTC</a>, from 3 to 100 lakh.
    </li>
  </ul>
</DocLayout>

<script>
  import { mountHike } from '../scripts/hike';
  mountHike();
</script>
